---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const guide = `${base}/guide/`;
const demo = `${base}/demo/`;
---
<Page title="Decision Ledger Setup | Your own journal site" description="Turn work notes into private, searchable journal site. Open source setup, your GitHub repo, your Cloudflare account.">
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Keep choices.<br />Find reasons.</h1>
        <p>Work moves on. Give decisions somewhere to stay. Turn Markdown notes into private, searchable journal site.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={guide}>Set up your site</a><a class="text-link" href={demo}>See sample journal</a></div>
        <p class="tiny">Open source code. Own GitHub and Cloudflare accounts. Real notes stay in your private repo.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="note-window" aria-label="Fake journal note showing recorder to site flow">
        <div class="window-bar"><span>decisions / search.md</span><span class="status">Fake sample</span></div>
        <div class="sample-note">
          <div class="note-meta">Nov 07, 2026 · search-service</div>
          <h2>Keep search close<br />to notes.</h2>
          <p><strong>Choice.</strong> Build search index with site.</p>
          <p><strong>Reason.</strong> Notes small. No separate search server to run or patch.</p>
          <p><strong>Next.</strong> Check results after next deploy.</p>
          <div class="tags">#decisions &nbsp; #search &nbsp; #small-tools</div>
        </div>
        <div class="note-bottom"><span>✓</span> Recorder saves Markdown<br /><span>✓</span> Private Git keeps history<br /><span>✓</span> Site build makes notes searchable</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap statement"><span><b aria-hidden="true">✓</b> Markdown stays source of truth</span><span><b aria-hidden="true">✓</b> Site code pinned to chosen commit</span><span><b aria-hidden="true">✓</b> Access login protects reads</span></div>
    <section class="section wrap" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="flow-title">From work session<br />to work record.</h2><p>Recorder writes notes. Private repo holds them. Setup code builds site. Each part has one clear job.</p></div>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow-item"><div class="step-label"><span>01 / capture</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></div><h3>Journal Recorder</h3><p>Save short summary from agent or manual input. Scrub known secret patterns before save.</p></div>
        <div class="flow-item"><div class="step-label"><span>02 / keep</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></div><h3>Private Git repo</h3><p>Markdown and history stay yours. Git sync pushes checked notes to chosen private repo.</p></div>
        <div class="flow-item"><div class="step-label"><span>03 / build</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></div><h3>Pinned setup code</h3><p>GitHub Actions fetches exact code version, then tests and builds pages from private notes.</p></div>
        <div class="flow-item"><div class="step-label"><span>04 / read</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h3>Your journal site</h3><p>Cloudflare Pages serves site. Access policy requires allowed login before readers see notes.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="features-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="features-title">Useful long after<br />session ends.</h2><p>Find why choice happened. Keep plain files you can read, move and edit with own tools.</p></div>
      <div class="ledger-row"><h3>Search across notes</h3><p>Search built journal without adding database. Entries link back to project context and earlier decisions.</p></div>
      <div class="ledger-row"><h3>Markdown you own</h3><p>Keep notes in Git, open same folder in Obsidian, or use text editor. Generated site never rewrites journal source.</p></div>
      <div class="ledger-row"><h3>Upgrade on your terms</h3><p>Private config pins full setup commit. Public code updates leave your site alone until you choose new version.</p></div>
      <div class="ledger-row"><h3>Archive, then restore</h3><p>Optional owner action moves notes within private repo. Add write access only when you need it. Reading works without write token.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap privacy" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <div><h2 id="privacy-title">Public code.<br />Private content.</h2><p>Privacy comes from repo visibility, host access rules and care with what you save. Public setup code alone cannot protect notes.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${guide}#4-set-privacy-and-first-deploy`}>Read privacy setup</a></div>
      <ul><li>Keep real journals and Git history in private repo. Both public repos hold code and fake examples only.</li><li>Protect production, preview and custom hosts with Cloudflare Access before real content upload.</li><li>Recorder filters known patterns. It cannot spot every private fact. Auto summaries still send scrubbed text to model service.</li><li>Keep tokens in private Actions secrets and Cloudflare runtime secrets. Never put them in site config or browser code.</li></ul>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <div><h2 id="start-title">Build your own record.</h2><p>One guide covers recorder, private repo, GitHub Actions and protected site. Already have site? Keep current clone and sync.</p></div><a class="button" href={guide}>Start setup guide</a>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">Before you start.</h2>
      <div>
        <details><summary>Does this publish my journals on GitHub Pages?</summary><p>No. This public Pages site holds setup guide and fake demo. Real journal site deploys to own Cloudflare Pages project behind Access. Real journal repo stays private.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need Journal Recorder?</summary><p>No. Write Markdown yourself or use existing recorder. Journal Recorder adds agent capture and checked Git sync. Site code reads Markdown either way.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Will local recorder mode update website?</summary><p>No. Local mode saves files on machine. Choose private repo clone and Git sync for automatic website updates.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does this need original author's accounts?</summary><p>No. Use own GitHub repo, Cloudflare account, domain and Access policy. Use public setup code directly or fork it.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Page>
